Description: enable V-Sync
 Call SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1) right after the OpenGL context is created,
 to avoid tearing. Animation is driven by SDL_GetTicks(), so the speed of
 the intro does not depend on the refresh rate.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
--- a/src/slsim.cpp
+++ b/src/slsim.cpp
@@ -529,6 +529,7 @@
 	SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_DEPTH_SIZE, 16);
 	sdlWindow = SDL_CreateWindow("Stochastic Lens Simulator by Gzrrplox",SDL_WINDOWPOS_CENTERED,SDL_WINDOWPOS_CENTERED,window_w,window_h,SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL);
 	SDL_GLContext sdlGlcontext = SDL_GL_CreateContext(sdlWindow);
+	SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1);
 	SDL_ShowCursor(0);
 
 	// Initialize framebuffer objects
